#LI-REMOTE

Headquarters:

Humane World for Animals

URL:

https://humaneworld.org

The general salary range for this full-time position is $80,000 – 115,000. Salary offers will be commensurate with experience, qualifications, skills, training and education.

Humane World for Animals, a global leader in animal advocacy and protection, is seeking a Web Developer, eCRM to support Digital Marketing and other departments by providing front-end, global web development solutions for fundraising, advocacy engagement, and other strategic priorities — incorporating AI-assisted and agentic development tools to accelerate delivery while maintaining rigorous human oversight, quality, and security standards.

Responsibilities:

Collaborates regularly with Digital Marketing, Brand and Visuals, and IS teams to discuss project requirements and makes technical recommendations. Writes efficient code and maintains custom donation forms, advocacy forms, other webpages, and email templates. Incorporates best practices for user experience, accessibility, page speed optimization, and GDPR compliance implementation. Adheres to global regulations and standards, regional data compliance, and security compliance;

Uses AI-assisted development tools and agentic coding assistants to accelerate coding, refactoring, debugging, testing, and documentation. Proactively identifies opportunities for AI-assisted and agent-built solutions and owns the ongoing maintenance, monitors their performance over time and updates or retires them as needed. Follows established guardrails and usage standards for AI tools and applies human-in-the-loop review to all AI-generated code and configurations, validating output for accuracy, security, accessibility, and brand/technical standards before deployment;

Follows quality assurance procedures and troubleshoots technical issues affecting donation forms, advocacy forms, webpages, and email templates in Engaging Networks. Works closely with vendor partners;

Works with the Information Security team to ensure that digital properties meet security standards, including managing script inventory, attestation, and other requirements for PCI compliance;

Collaborates with the testing team to gather testing requirements and implement new features to run A/B and multivariate tests on forms;

Creates and maintains clear and concise documentation of custom web development, support guides, and incident reports;

Performs other duties as assigned.

Qualifications and Requirements:

Bachelor's degree in computer programming, web development, or related field, or equivalent work experience required;

A minimum of four (4) years of experience in front-end web development and developing custom websites required;

Demonstrated experience with Engaging Networks or other eCRMs;

Proficient in HTML5, Sass and CSS, JavaScript, PHP, MySQL, GitHub, Engaging Networks modules, Webpack, Node, npm, core AWS services, and Mailgun. Familiar with Segment or other CDPs;

Direct experience with AI coding assistants and agentic development tools such as Microsoft Copilot Studio, Claude Code, and GitHub Copilot;

Knowledge of best practices for responsive, mobile-first web design, UX, accessibility, page speed optimization, browser support, and GDPR compliance;

Familiar with cookie consent tools, preferably Iubenda, for configuring compliance settings;

Experience building interactive data visualizations that translate campaigns into compelling stories for supporters to increase engagement;

Excellent attention to detail when coding projects based on Adobe XD files or Figma;

Understanding of digital marketing strategies for US and international audiences;

Stays on top of AI trends in web development, including personalization and workflow automation, and their responsible application to fundraising and advocacy technology;

Strong written and verbal communication skills;

Must be able to multi-task in a fast-paced, collaborative environment to deliver high quality work on deadline. Familiarity with Jira and Confluence a plus;

Data informed problem solver having experience with A/B testing platforms and Google Analytics;

Proactive and ability to work both independently and as an effective team member in a team environment;

Interest in animal protection issues preferred.

This is a full-time remote position based in the United States. Candidates must be able to accomodate Eastern Time hours, as needed.

Q

ualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, and disability, marital or parental status or protected veteran status.  EOE

To apply:

https://weworkremotely.com/remote-jobs/humane-world-for-animals-web-designer-ecrm-1

Bosch Digital – Тogether we shape tomorrow

We are Bosch Digital and we drive IT and digital business within Bosch.

What we do

We are the digital pioneers within Bosch. Our competitive portfolio, deep understanding of Bosch needs, and long-standing expertise make us the go-to destination for accelerating IT and digital business. We work with and for almost all Bosch units. We foster a customer-centric, agile software culture that attracts digital talents and gives people and ideas room to grow. Bosch Digital supports and consults the entire Bosch Group with all its business units in implementing digital business and scalable solutions - and in marketing and selling them successfully to their customers and partners.

Who we are

Our full set of consulting and implementation skills enables us to drive IT and digital projects from the first idea to the market release. With our agile mindset and working culture, we are a key driver of digital transformation at Bosch.

Your future colleagues include solution architects and cloud software developers, UX and business model designers, digital marketers, consultants, and project managers in a diverse team.

We are as international as our customers and work in interdisciplinary teams at locations all over the world.

As an HR Associate / Payroll Specialist, you will play a key role in ensuring the accuracy, efficiency, and compliance of our payroll and HR operations.

You will work closely with internal teams and external partners to support seamless payroll processes, maintain high-quality employee data, and contribute to the smooth execution of core HR activities.

In our fast-paced, people-centered environment, your attention to detail, time management and structured approach will be essential in delivering reliable processes and supporting a consistent employee experience.

Your contribution to something big:

Payroll Management

Process monthly payroll accurately and on time;

Maintain payroll records, including salaries, bonuses, deductions, and benefits;

Prepare payroll-related reports and documentation to support a smooth payroll process;

Contribute to the development and implementation of payroll policies and procedures in line with best practices and regulatory requirements;

Support employees with payroll-related questions and concerns.

HR Administration

Maintain accurate employee records and HR databases;

Support onboarding and offboarding processes;

Prepare employment contracts, amendments, and HR documentation;

Manage and track employee absences and leave balances;

Assist in the maintenance and continuous improvement of HR policies and procedures.

Compliance & Reporting

Ensure compliance with labor laws, internal policies, and regulatory requirements;

Support audits and compliance reviews by providing accurate documentation and information;

Generate and manage HR and payroll reports, ensuring timely and accurate data across functions;

Collaborate with global HR teams to ensure consistency, alignment, and compliance.

What distinguishes you:

Bachelor's or Master's degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, or a related field;

Proven experience in an HR Administration, ideally in a fast-paced, international environment;

Strong knowledge of payroll processes and labor legislation;

Familiarity with local HR policies and legal requirements;

Comfortable working with HR analytics and reporting tools. SAP Success Factors is a plus;

Strong working knowledge of Microsoft Office applications, especially Excel and Word, with the ability to use them effectively in a professional environment;

Excellent attention to detail, organizational skills, communication and interpersonal skills;

Fluent in English; other languages are a plus.

What do we offer:

Very competitive remuneration package;

Personal training plan (annual goals and budget);

Collaborate with colleagues and teams from around the globe;

Open and friendly working atmosphere, stable work environment, positive office culture, availability to work from home;

Inspiring Atmosphere and innovative projects;

Work in a well-established and growing international company;

A variety of additional benefits like Multisport card, food vouchers, public transport card and many more.

You think you have unique qualifications that make you the ideal candidate for us? Simply send us your resume.

Please note that only candidates approved by CV will be contacted!

Technology is our how. And people are our why. For over two decades, we have been harnessing technology to drive meaningful change.

By combining world-class engineering, industry expertise and a people-centric mindset, we consult and partner with leading brands from various industries to create dynamic platforms and intelligent digital experiences that drive innovation and transform businesses.

From prototype to real-world impact - be part of a global shift by doing work that matters.

The procurement team sources and acquires essential goods and services, negotiates contracts, and manages vendor relationships to ensure quality and cost-effectiveness. They coordinate with departments to understand needs, maintain inventory, and oversee logistics, supporting the seamless functioning of the company's IT infrastructure.

Responsibilities:

Conduct vendor due diligence for regular and M&A suppliers;

Manage contracts, track renewals, and ensure compliance with procurement requirements;

Collaborate with Oracle consultants to deliver comprehensive solutions;

Support project teams with procurement needs and transfer knowledge to new business teams;

Assist with the implementation and adoption of new procurement systems;

Identify and address inefficiencies and opportunities for process automation;

Develop reports and compile data based on business needs;

Resolve contract-related issues and act as a contact point between the organization and suppliers;

Perform SOX controls and ensure compliance with SOX requirements;

Provide updates and information to customers on changes and known issues;

Stay informed about industry trends and support management in sourcing strategies;

Offer back-up support to the Procurement Team as needed.

Excellent procurement knowledge and at least 1 years of experience;

Exceptional attention to detail and a thorough, conscientious work ethic;

Strong customer care and service orientation in interactions with peers and suppliers;

